WEBVTT

00:00:01,100 --> 00:00:10,100
Hi, my name is Patty Wilson, and I was diagnosed with stage 4 non-Hodgkin's lymphoma in October of 2017.

00:00:11,100 --> 00:00:20,100
My oncologist did not choose to do any treatment at the time because it would make me sick and I was not feeling sick at that time.

00:00:21,100 --> 00:00:26,100
In early 2018, I did start getting signs and symptoms of the disease progressing.

00:00:26,100 --> 00:00:36,100
So, I began looking into complementary or integrative cancer care, and after much research, I found Conner's clinic.

00:00:37,100 --> 00:00:46,100
Conner's clinic made the most sense for me for what I needed, and I've been very grateful that I went there every sense.

00:00:46,100 --> 00:01:09,100
I continue to be supported by Conner's clinic. I do still see my conventional medicine oncologist, but fortunately my cancer has been stable since April of last May of 2018.

00:01:10,100 --> 00:01:20,100
Everything was stable, I had new testing, blood, and CAT scans done in November 2018, and everything remains stable.

00:01:21,100 --> 00:01:30,100
So, if you want really great integrative care, and that's compassionate, you should come to Conner's clinic.

